  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly identified the episode as a ventral incisional hernia awaiting elective laparoscopic repair with full anesthesia. All seven minimum responsibility‐chain items were met without any serious error. No high‐order point was fully activated, triggered and completed with case‐specific beyond‐minimum action; HO4 comes closest but partially reuses the same safety‐closure content already required for RC7 and the closure contract, and the other HO items remained not triggered or not completed. Therefore the trajectory stays at the acceptable boundary with no in‐chain error but no completed high‐order point.",
